{"id":"be9d6cafebcc4c1b","group":"17","path":"17/17-thm-special-model-existence.md","title":"Existence of a Special Model","display":"thm-special-model-existence — Existence of a Special Model","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-thm-special-model-existence","aliases":["17-thm-special-model-existence"],"display":"thm-special-model-existence — Existence of a Special Model","depends_on":["[[17-df-special-model]]","[[17-df-model]]","[[17-df-cardinal-arithmetic]]","[[17-df-language-cardinality]]"],"source_section":"5.1","source_result":"Propositions 5.1.7(i) and 5.1.8","source_pages_print":[296],"source_pages_djvu":[312],"source_verification":"statement and successor/limit construction proof compared in supplied OCR; local theory-level corollary","label_origin":"local-catalog","legacy_label":"17-thm-5.2.2","local_revision":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-thm-special-model-existence"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-thm-special-model-existence</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-special-model-existence — Existence of a Special Model"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"8a4d6bb923655efc\" href=\"?note=8a4d6bb923655efc\" title=\"17-df-special-model\">17-df-special-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"e8f9375543fc2e7d\" href=\"?note=e8f9375543fc2e7d\" title=\"17-df-language-cardinality\">17-df-language-cardinality</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_section","html":"5.1"},{"key":"source_result","html":"Propositions 5.1.7(i) and 5.1.8"},{"key":"source_pages_print","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>296</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pages_djvu","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>312</span></div>"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"statement and successor/limit construction proof compared in supplied OCR; local theory-level corollary"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-thm-5.2.2"},{"key":"local_revision","html":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> 为候选集合。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span> is an <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-theory; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\">\\(\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\)</span> is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Special}_\\kappa\">\\(\\operatorname{Special}_\\kappa\\)</span> is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"8a4d6bb923655efc\" href=\"?note=8a4d6bb923655efc\" title=\"17-df-special-model\">17-df-special-model</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\)</span> is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_0\">\\(\\aleph_0\\)</span> is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|L|\">\\(|L|\\)</span> is the language-symbol cardinality from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"e8f9375543fc2e7d\" href=\"?note=e8f9375543fc2e7d\" title=\"17-df-language-cardinality\">17-df-language-cardinality</a>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bigl||\\mathfrak M|\\bigr|\">\\(\\bigl||\\mathfrak M|\\bigr|\\)</span> denotes the cardinality of the carrier.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\aleph_0\\leq\\kappa\\land|L|&lt;\\kappa\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\Bigl[\\forall\\beta&lt;\\kappa\\;(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\beta)\\to 2^\\beta\\leq\\kappa)\\Bigr]\n\\land\\exists\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n(\\aleph_0\\leq\\bigl||\\mathfrak M|\\bigr|&lt;\\kappa)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\exists\\mathfrak A\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\operatorname{Special}_\\kappa(\\mathfrak A).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\aleph_0\\leq\\kappa\\land|L|&lt;\\kappa\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\Bigl[\\forall\\beta&lt;\\kappa\\;(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\beta)\\to 2^\\beta\\leq\\kappa)\\Bigr]\n\\land\\exists\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n(\\aleph_0\\leq\\bigl||\\mathfrak M|\\bigr|&lt;\\kappa)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\exists\\mathfrak A\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\operatorname{Special}_\\kappa(\\mathfrak A).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>This is the theory-level consequence of Proposition 5.1.8, printed p.296, DjVu page 312. Proposition 5.1.7(i) identifies the displayed power-set bound with the book's condition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa=\\kappa^*\">\\(\\kappa=\\kappa^*\\)</span>. Proposition 5.1.8 constructs a special elementary extension of the displayed infinite model of cardinality below <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>; elementary extension preserves <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>. Its proof treats successor and limit cardinals separately and does not require <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> to be regular. The local label is not the book proposition number.</p>\n<p>The earlier hypotheses were insufficient. A complete theory of a finite structure has no infinite model at all. Also <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega^{&lt;\\omega}=\\omega\">\\(\\omega^{&lt;\\omega}=\\omega\\)</span> cannot guarantee a countable special model: the complete theory of countably many independent unary predicates has continuum many complete <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"1\">\\(1\\)</span>-types. The strict language bound and the displayed source condition avoid both errors.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-special-model","status":"resolved","id":"8a4d6bb923655efc","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-special-model]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-model","status":"resolved","id":"53255a372e5c1ee8","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-model]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic","status":"resolved","id":"0c4